# CHANGELOG

LEGEND:
Development version <VERSION x.x.x> - <DATE> yyyy-mm-dd - Specifies latest version, not current changes in this codebase. use UNRELEASED for the date if that is the case

Development version Beta 0.9.1 - 2026-02-01 
--------------------------------------------
- Deployed application for first round of playtesting
- No currently known issues with this build
- Optimized Build Script to remove internal assets after build completion

Development version Beta 0.9.2 - 2026-02-03 
-------------------------------------------
- Overhauled LeaderboardViewer to use a state machine for fetching data for better management of state
- Prettied up UI in leaderboard
- Removed the last vestiges of pygame from outside core/guts
- Began implementing the Keys class in core/guts/input to map keys for the framework and input manager.
    - This will make future updates to the controls system much smoother, and will allow for custom input behavior (i.e. capital letters, custom characters, and more)
- Revamped build system separately for windows and linux, you still need a bash shell for windows though
- Added a file for tracking feature requests as well as a file for tracking active bugs
- Added a NEW SYSTEM for updating the application at the click of a button 
- Added updater executable that gets created at build time so that the game can update

Development version Beta 0.9.3 - 2026-02-04
--------------------------------------------

- Fixed a bug where linux builds would not start if they were running a version of python previous to 3.12
    - Mainly due to an issue where newer versions of python allow f strings to use """" rather than "''", which while handy as a feature
    - Causes ungodly compatibility issues
- Fixed a bug where the PLAYER_POWER_STATE was being set to PowerUpType.TYPE, which is a totally impossible transition.
    - logging for invalid state transitions is paying dividends now

- Made button hover UI more uniform setting a standard color for text when mouse is hovering over a button
    - active buttons will have text that turns PURPLE when hovering and will change the program state to whatever that button does
    - inactive buttons will have text that turns GREY when hovering and will not change anything in the program state

- Added button to link to the website from the game
- Made update button pop out and more obvious with contrasting background color and added text near the title indicating update availability
- Set alpha value on button surfaces (this should have been done months ago)
- Set max volume to 5 and changed default volume to 3
- Made tutorial prompts check the actual key bindings to tell the player how to play

Development version Beta 0.9.4 - 2026-02-05
-------------------------------------------
- Added to the splash screen system and introduced game mechanics in the loading screen
- Fixed a bug where entities would artifact at the top left hand corner of the screen
    - This bug was around for quite some time. Zap you go
- Made player's username flash if they are on the leaderboard
- Renamed APPMODE to DEBUG_STATE and rehandled it as a debug overlay state manager
    - Basically, the debug overlay shows active states (next part of this upgrade) and can be toggled
    - Eventually I will be adding OS info, as well as hardware info. Preparing this for larger games.
- Put all environment specific logic into an `example.config.py` and made `setup.py` to load the real config file for the dev
- Added a score multiplier
- Added new entity type: Multiplier Upgrade
- Added masking for player collisions
- Added Multiplier Upgrade section to Tutorial Mode
- Implemented a half baked daylight cycle that is not ready for the game.

Development version Beta 0.9.5 - 2026-02-05
--------------------------------------------

- HOTFIX No username creation possible. -FIXED

Development version Beta 0.9.6 - 2026-02-08
--------------------------------------------

- Added Speed Boost powerup
- Added the ability to slow the player down by holding shift
- Added SPEED_STATE for managing player speed (SLOW,NORMAL,FAST)
- Added API key on both client and server to maintain database integrity
- Added system to show latest changelog upon updating, but only then

Development version Beta 0.9.7 - 2026-02-11
--------------------------------------------
- Set timer to 0 every time you have to restart the game/go to menu
- Fixed state bug where the program would skip asking the user for a leaderboard opt in
- Fixed issue where if user chooses the same username with a fresh client, their high score will pull from the server immediately
- Made changelog screen split up lines
- Added error handling properly without pesky print statements
- Removed Multiplier Upgrade entity and replaced the multiplier system
- Multiplier increases by 1 every 10 levels now
- You can now press enter to submit your username and not just the submit button

Development version Beta 0.9.8 - 2026-07-08
--------------------------------------------
- Overhauled handling of core systems (rendering,audio,input)
- Fixed tutorial mode's lack of ability to be completed.
- Added a centralized list of active states that can be queryed by any state machine from anywhere that has one
- Made LoFiSi the only song that plays at the main menu
- Added readme in build scripts
- Added instructions in build scripts
- Added license file to build scripts - it was accessible via the website which you could get to via the game client, but this is just to comply even more accurately with the license.
- Added feature for drawing color coded lines from the player to the entities in developer mode. This can be accessed with F3, F4, F5, F6
- Added focused observability of global active states. You can now toggle between viewing active state types in the debug overlay with F8+1,2,3,4.
- You can now see your username and high score at the main menu.
- Fixed all bugs around changing username/reloading client
- Opting out of leaderboard sets username to "Player" and only handles local high score data
- Added a Day/Night cycle with brightness values
- Added temperature mechanic
- Added Sun (rising/setting with time and increasing temperature)
- Player snowball now shrinks faster depending on temperature
- Updated to latest version of Distant Realms Framework

Development version Beta 0.9.9 - 2026-07-27
--------------------------------------------
- Added Snow Blitz debug utilities class
- Added support for multiple text boxes and passwords
- Added UI manager that will eventually house the entire UI system allowing for editor level construction of menus
- Added full support for authenticated user accounts, and properly built a network stack as part of the runtime
- Ported new framework features back into the Distant Realms repo and then made more runtime level changes back into this repo
- APPSTATE is now RUNTIME_STATE and now only serves as a lifecycle state definition rather than an app state definition.
- Updated UI system to allow for scrollables. Leaderboard now shows entire leaderboard.
- Improved player size by tying it to a normalized size and calculating based on that
- Smoother growing
- Day cycle is twice as long and fully includes a night cycle as well
- Added seasons
- Added days
- Added years
- Added the start of a weather system
- Added extensible environment system
- Updated to Distant Realms version 0.3.0-alpha
- Abstracted UI even more allowing for widgets, composables (forms/maybe menus in the future), and a simple UI manager for composables
- Fixed client crashing upon initialization when no audio device is found
-- Old immediate mode menus still exist
